.TH LLAMA2C 1 "2026-11-17" "llama2.c" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
llama2c, llama2c\-q8 \- run a small Llama 2 language model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B llama2c
.I model.bin
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B llama2c\-q8
.I model_q80.bin
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B llama2c
is llama2.c (https://github.com/karpathy/llama2.c) by Andrej Karpathy, an inference engine for the Llama 2 architecture in one C file. It reads a model in the format of that project
and continues a text (the prompt) one token at a time. With the small TinyStories models it writes simple children's stories.
.B llama2c\-q8
is the same for models quantized to int8 (version 2 of the format, made by export.py of the project).
.PP
A model has to fit in the memory of the phone: the engine reads all the weights for every token. stories15M (61 MB) runs at about 3 tokens per second on the N900; stories42M (167 MB) does not fit
and takes half a minute per token.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " temperature"
the temperature, from 0 (always the likeliest token) up; default 1.0.
.TP
.BI \-p " p"
the p of top\-p (nucleus) sampling, 0 to 1; default 0.9.
.TP
.BI \-s " seed"
the random seed; default the time.
.TP
.BI \-n " steps"
the number of tokens to generate; default 256; 0 is the length of the context of the model.
.TP
.BI \-i " prompt"
the beginning of the text.
.TP
.BI \-z " tokenizer"
a tokenizer file other than
.I tokenizer.bin
in the current directory. The package has
.I /opt/llama2c/share/llama2c/tokenizer.bin
for the models of Llama 2 size, and
.I tok512.bin
for stories260K.
.TP
.BI \-m " mode"
.B generate
(the default) or
.BR chat .
.TP
.BI \-y " text"
a system prompt in the chat mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
llama2c /opt/llama2c/share/llama2c/stories260K.bin \e
    \-z /opt/llama2c/share/llama2c/tok512.bin \-i "Once upon a time" \-n 100
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llama\-story (1),
.BR n900 (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrej Karpathy (MIT licence). The package for the N900: https://github.com/n900\-resurrection
